{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"astrakhan-sylphish-imago","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nStory quilted-nepotic-kitty (9835-95f2-3072-4dc1) deletes `src/rebar/schemas/check_mcp_models.py`, and its plan also deleted the ruff per-file ignore `\"src/rebar/schemas/check_mcp_models.py\" = [\"T201\"]` (`pyproject.toml:583`). Any change that edits `pyproject.toml` is a dependency-map change, so the Gerrit pip-audit lane (`scripts/dependency_audit.py`, \"if you touch it, you own it\") blocks it on the outstanding main advisories tracked by unhelpful-supersmart-chrysalis (f7dc-132b-057a-476c). Change 3045 got `Verified -1` for exactly that. The story therefore leaves the line in place; it is inert (ruff ignores a per-file entry whose path does not exist) but stale config.\n\n## Approach\nDelete the one line `\"src/rebar/schemas/check_mcp_models.py\" = [\"T201\"]` from `[tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores]` in `pyproject.toml`. Land it only once unhelpful-supersmart-chrysalis is closed (the lane no longer blocks), or bundle it into the change that remediates those advisories, since that change already owns `uv.lock`/`pyproject.toml`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `grep -n check_mcp_models pyproject.toml` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `make lint` and the Gerrit pip-audit lane pass for the change.","id":"898b-f66b-0fed-4d31","parent_id":"04f1-5f92-3119-4731","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Drop the stale ruff per-file ignore for the deleted check_mcp_models.py from pyproject.toml"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792389557372303223,"uuid":"9be333bf-2ef3-44f8-851b-94ad5df29b4f"}